Root Cause
The Failed to load workspace data SyntaxError: Unexpected token '<', "<html><hea"... is not valid JSON error occurred because:
In Vite development mode (middlewareMode: true with appType: 'spa'), any unmatched /api/* route fell through to Vite's SPA handler, which returned the HTML index.html document instead of a JSON response.
In the frontend API service, res.json() directly attempted to parse the returned HTML payload without verifying the Content-Type header, causing the SyntaxError: Unexpected token '<'.
Parameter matching in /api/workspace/mailbox and /api/workspace/applications required flexible code aliases (30072012, Master, or query parameter variations).
Changes Implemented
API Fallback & Global Error Handlers (server.ts):
Added an explicit app.all('/api/*', ...) route handler prior to Vite's middleware, guaranteeing that any unmatched API request strictly returns a clean JSON 404 object ({ success: false, message: 'API route not found' }) and never leaks HTML.
Added a global Express error handler for /api/* to catch any exceptions and return clean JSON 500 error objects.
Updated executive authentication to recognize both master code 30072012 and the Master token alias across /api/workspace/mailbox, /api/workspace/applications, /api/workspace/projects/:id, and /api/workspace/projects/cleanup.
Resilient JSON Fetch Wrapper (src/services/workspaceApi.ts & src/services/api.ts):
Implemented safeFetchJson<T>, which inspects the Content-Type header before parsing.
If an unexpected non-JSON response or gateway status occurs, it safely falls back to standard empty structures (e.g. empty lists or failure indicators) and logs a diagnostic warning rather than throwing an unhandled SyntaxError.
Workspace Data Ingestion (AdminDashboard.tsx & MembersWorkspace.tsx):
Added array safety guards (setMembers(mems || []), etc.) so that all UI state remains stable during live polling cycles.
